  "id": "motor-end-plate",
  "term": "motor end plate",
  "definition": "The motor end plate is the specialized part of a muscle cell located directly opposite the end of a motor neuron across the synaptic gap. It contains structural folds and a high concentration of cholinergic receptors that help receive nerve signals.",
